# Loading states and skeletons

## Prefer skeletons for structured content

- For **lists, cards, tables, and dashboards**, use **skeleton placeholders** that mirror the **final layout** (same grid, spacing, border radius, and approximate heights) instead of a generic spinner-only state.
- Use existing design tokens: `bg-surface-*`, `border-border`, `rounded-xl` (or match the real component), and **`animate-pulse`** on skeleton blocks (see [`src/components/ui/Skeleton.tsx`](src/components/ui/Skeleton.tsx)).

## Accessibility

- Mark the loading region with **`aria-busy="true"`** while fetching, and **`aria-live="polite"`** when content will replace the skeleton.
- Provide an **`aria-label`** (e.g. “Loading workspaces”) on the skeleton container so screen readers announce purpose.

## Scope loading UI

- Avoid replacing the **entire page** with a spinner if headers or static chrome can stay visible; skeleton only the **async section** (e.g. workspace grid on the dashboard).

## Revalidation

- After **create/update** actions, a **short refetch** may use a lighter pattern (inline spinner on the button, or optimistic UI) so the full skeleton does not flash unless the list was empty or a hard reload is intended.
